WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.540
Good morning John.

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:10.660
This may have been the second oddest weekend of my life.

00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:15.060
I perused Portland real estate with a Mythbuster's wife on an iPad owned by Adam Savage.

00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:20.700
Yes you can say that my perception of reality was ravaged. But imagine, that wasn't even the weirdest bit.

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:23.020
And you're gonna **** a brick when you hear the rest of it.

00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:28.200
So sit down and listen to me rhythmically talk about the weekend that I participated in w00tstock.

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:32.720
Now I'm on a plane home and I just want to remember it - hearing Adam Savage saying that he likes my music.

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:37.340
And I've been listening to Frontalot - 200 tracks back to back which is probably why I wrote out this song as a rap

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:42.380
but I hope whoever sits in 9D next doesn't gag because I'm writing down these lyrics on the back of a barf bag.

00:00:42.380 --> 00:00:47.840
For me, it began when I landed in Seattle at 2 o'clock and then I had 3 hours talking with the king of nerd hip hop.

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:52.680
MC Frontalot, as he's professionally known, could probably cure cancer with his headlamp and a microphone.

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:57.540
And then Molly walked in with her adorable grin and her boyfriend Chris and her assistant Kristin.

00:00:57.540 --> 00:01:01.880
Two girls, one uke, don't fear, it won't make you puke unless you're easily nauseated by things abnormally cute.

00:01:01.880 --> 00:01:07.420
And then I felt that I was losing control of my brain because the drummer of the Presidents of the USA

00:01:07.420 --> 00:01:12.740
was hanging with me, making jokes, telling me to be strong, like he jumped straight out of my tape player and into my song.

00:01:12.740 --> 00:01:17.000
And then my friend Stephen Toulouse walked by. He decides who lives and dies on Xbox Live..

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:21.960
He's the guy with the ban hammer on the largest gaming platform. And we were all brought here by messers Paul and Storm

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:26.740
who were in good form and bought the pizza that I was eatin' when I learned just how nerdy was the nerd Wil Wheaton.

00:01:26.780 --> 00:01:33.920
He was adorably excited, jumping up and down. His smile was the inverse function of a frown, taken to 1024th power.

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:39.100
I did my best not to fangirl for the whole next hour. And then I was on the stage ostensibly earning my wage.

00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:41.100
Picard had thrown me into overdrive and said "engage".

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:43.840
My cheeks hurt from laughing, it was so much freaking fun.

00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:47.420
Savage, Fraction, Frontalot and Loading Ready Run and then done.

00:01:47.420 --> 00:01:53.400
And we were up there taking our bow, like wow, the crowd's so loud that I could not understand how this had happened to me, I mean I'm just another geek.

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:58.380
Well last week, it had a freaking unique streak. Just a couple of days ago the world was planting me trees

00:01:58.380 --> 00:02:01.280
and now I'm up in front of a thousand geeks living my dreams.

00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:05.860
I'm prepared to accept this is the pinnacle of my career, I don't mind if it's all downhill from here

00:02:05.860 --> 00:02:10.840
because here's a pretty good place to be downhill from, I mean there's an awful lot of hill there before you hit the bottom.

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:15.640
And in the morning, my goodness, I saw that Wil Wheaton had pulled out his Blackberry and done some tweeting.

00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:20.500
He tweeted I killed it and from what he could hear my set, of all of those at w00tstock, got the biggest cheer.

00:02:20.500 --> 00:02:25.520
I'm not really concerned about whether this is true or not, it just makes me pretty grateful there's a thing call w00tstock.

00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:29.340
Yeah, w00tstock.

00:02:30.260 --> 00:02:34.320
It's a rap that I did about w00tstock.

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:37.780
And the beat, the beat is, the beat just keeps going?

00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:39.880
When do I stop?

00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:44.000
I-I don't have any more words... O-Okay

00:02:44.860 --> 00:02:47.640
John, how is this my life?

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:53.720
The show went really well, if I do say so myself. Everyone was hilarious the whole time and my part went well too.

00:02:53.720 --> 00:02:57.700
So I'm putting the link in my pants down here so that you can go check it out.

00:02:57.700 --> 00:03:01.560
And there will also be an annotation at the end of the video, which is just about right now.

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:08.300
So John, I will see you on Friday in which you answer some awesome Nerdfighter questions. Bye bye!

